teger \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) and choose the following\n\\(n\\) lines:\n\n\\[\n\\mathcal L_k=\\{D_0,D_1,\\dots ,D_{k-1}\\}\\cup\\{V_1,V_2,\\dots ,V_{\\,n-k}\\}.\n\\]\n\nThe first \\(k\\) members are sunny, the remaining \\(n-k\\) are non‑sunny, and\nall are distinct; thus \\(|\\mathcal L_k|=n\\).\n\nWe prove that every point of \\(\\mathcal P\\) belongs to at least one line of\n\\(\\mathcal L_k\\).\n\nLet \\((a,b)\\in\\mathcal P\\) and set \\(c=b-a\\).\n\n*Case 1: \\(c\\le k-1\\).*  \nThen \\((a,b)\\in D_c\\) and \\(D_c\\) is one of the chosen sunny lines.\n\n*Case 2: \\(c\\ge k\\).*  \nFrom the defining inequality \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) we obtain  \n\n\\[\na\\le\\frac{n+1-c}{2}\\le\\frac{n+1-k}{2}\\le n-k .\n\\]\n\n(The last inequality holds because \\(k\\le n\\) and \\(n\\ge3\\).)  \nThus \\(a\\) is an integer with \\(1\\le a\\le n-k\\), so the vertical line\n\\(V_a\\) (which is among the chosen non‑sunny lines) contains \\((a,b)\\).\n\nIn both cases the point is covered, proving that the family \\(\\mathcal L_k\\)\nsatisfies the required covering condition.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3. Final answer\n\nWe have shown\n\n* a necessary condition \\(k\\le n\\);\n* for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) an explicit construction of\n  \\(n\\) distinct lines, exactly \\(k\\) of which are sunny, that covers all\n  points \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a+b\\le n+1\\).\n\nHence the set of all admissible values of \\(k\\) is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
