uration contains exactly \\(n\\) lines, the number of sunny lines cannot exceed \\(n\\).  \nTherefore no \\(k>n\\) is possible.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**Final answer:** for every integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the admissible values of \\(k\\) are precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0,1,2,\\dots ,n}.\n\\]"
