nct members.\n\nSince \\(|E|=\\bigl\\lfloor n/2\\bigr\\rfloor\\), by choosing \\(S\\) of any cardinality \\(k\\) with  \n\n\\[\n0\\le k\\le\\Bigl\\lfloor\\frac{n}{2}\\Bigr\\rfloor ,\n\\tag{13}\n\\]\n\nwe obtain a configuration satisfying the two conditions of the problem and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.  Conclusion  \n\nThe necessary condition (10) and the constructive family (12) together show that the admissible values of \\(k\\) are precisely the integers from \\(0\\) up to \\(\\bigl\\lfloor n/2\\bigr\\rfloor\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k\\in\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,\\bigl\\lfloor \\tfrac{n}{2}\\bigr\\rfloor\\}\\;}\n\\]"
